title: Marigold — a compass vehicle on admitting water (ADR-366 D5c, D5g, D6)
story: vehicles
description: Steered north at a pace of two turns the Marigold crosses the
  Open Water region, which admits it, and stops at the Shoal, which does not.
  A save made under way restores the heading and the step count so the next
  step lands on schedule. The anchor stops it from a story clause.

---

> north
[OK: contains "Depot"]

> east
[OK: contains "Harbour"]

> enter marigold
[OK: contains "get into the Marigold"]

# pace: 2 turns — the steer turn's tick counts; the step lands next turn
> steer north
[OK: contains "You steer the Marigold north."]
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

# Under way with one tick to go: save here
$save marigold-under-way

> wait
[OK: contains "The Marigold arrives at the Sound."]

# Restore mid-step: heading and step count ride the save, so the same wait arrives
$restore marigold-under-way

> wait
[OK: contains "The Marigold arrives at the Sound."]

> wait
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

> wait
[OK: contains "The Marigold arrives at the Strait."]

# The Shoal does not admit the Marigold: the heading clears and it stops, once
> wait
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

> wait
[OK: contains "The Marigold comes to a stop."]
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

> look
[OK: contains "Strait"]

> wait
[OK: not contains "stop"]

# Steered back, then stopped from a story clause before the step lands
> steer south
[OK: contains "You steer the Marigold south."]

> pull anchor
[OK: contains "The anchor goes over the side"]

> wait
[OK: not contains "arrives"]

> look
[OK: contains "Strait"]
